      "writtenOn": "2023-05-12T10:35:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good question! It was very tricky. There are two kinds of boot images: some are produced by bootclasspath_fragments (specificially, \"art\"), and some are produced by platform_bootclasspath (specifically, \"boot\" and \"mainline\").\n\n- For those produced by bootclasspath_fragments:\n  - If `installDirOnDevice` starts with \"apex/\", always install to `javalib/\u003cisa\u003e` of the APEX regardless of the rest of the string.\n  - Otherwise, install to the location specified by `installDirOnDevice`\n- For those produced by platform_bootclasspath:\n  - Always install to `installDirOnHost` regardless of `installDirOnDevice`\n\nBeside, boot images produced by bootclasspath_fragments will not be installable after aosp/2585513, so `installDirOnDevice` for those configs will have no effect.",
      "parentUuid": "b0eae149_97abac95",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 9,
        "endChar": 56
      },
